        "##### 10. What is the difference between a decision tree and a set of bagged decision trees? Be specific and precise!\n",
        "\n",
        "• Quantity: A decision tree is one single tree, while bagging uses multiple parallel trees.\n",
        "\n",
        "• Stability: A single tree is unstable and overfits easily; bagging is stable and reduces errors.\n",
        "\n",
        "• A single tree gives you one path's result; bagging combines the answers of all trees to get a safer average.\n"
      ]
